[187.844805, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[0m \u001b[2mopticli\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[191.844805, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mcd /demo/Alloy; opticli search \"Alloy Track whitepaper\" --in strings; opticli search \"whitepaper\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[195.725321, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mcd /demo/Alloy; opticli where-used 104 --pages; opticli where-used 8 --pages; opticli type TeaserBlock; opticli get 104\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[199.725321, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mcd /demo/Alloy; opticli get 9 --fields MainContentArea --full; opticli get 7 --fields MainContentArea --full; grep -rn \"TeaserBlo\u001b[2m…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[202.469173, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mcd /demo/Alloy; opticli get 9 --fields MainContentArea --full; opticli get 7 --fields MainContentArea --full\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[203.000513, "o", "  \u001b[36m●\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mgrep -rn \"TeaserBlockWide\\|\\\"wide\\\"\\|Wide\" --include=*.cs --include=*.cshtml /demo/Alloy | grep -v /obj/ | head -20\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[207.000513, "o", "\r\n  Two pages promote the Alloy Track whitepaper (`/en/alloy-track/download-whitepaper-alloy-track/`, content 8):\r\n  \r\n  - **Alloy Meet** (`/en/alloy-meet/`, content 9) is the new one. Its `MainContentArea` holds the new block \"Alloy Track whitepaper teaser\" (content 104,\r\n    heading \"Plan less, ship more\"). opticli added it today, 2026-09-29, and it's published.\r\n  - **Alloy Track** (`/en/alloy-track/`, content 7) has had it since 2021. It doesn't use the teaser block: it puts the whitepaper page itself in\r\n    `MainContentArea` with the \"full\" display option, so it shows as a wide page partial (`PageWide.cshtml`).\r\n  \r\n  The new teaser is rendered by:\r\n  - **C# class:** `Alloy.Models.Blocks.TeaserBlock` in `Models/Blocks/TeaserBlock.cs:11`.\r\n"]
[207.000586, "o", "  - **Razor view:** `Views/Shared/Blocks/TeaserBlock.cshtml`. On Alloy Meet the teaser has no display option, so it gets the default view. The other view,\r\n    `TeaserBlockWide.cshtml`, is only used for the \"wide\" and \"full\" display options (set in `Business/Rendering/TemplateCoordinator.cs:42`).\r\n"]
[211.000586, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m/demo/Alloy\u001b[0m \u001b[36m❯\u001b[0m o"]
